The tales of Galanda the priest

This story was inspired by Krysia's Krusader and the Saga of Ellora. I
do not hope to be anywhere as inventive and interesting as her, and if
you're reading Krysia, you're my nethack idol! :-)

***This story will contain a lot of spoilers! Do not read on if
apposed to spoilers!***

This story is based on a real nethack game. Heck, it is the real story
of Galanda, who still lives on in the dungeons today. Unfortunetly,
some specifics (such as shop prices, exact amount of hits taken from a
monster etc) will not be correct (I don't take any notes). This story
is going to be quite long, possibly longer even than the saga of
Ellora (if I survive that long! :-)), so if you just want a
five-minute read, don't bother. However if you don't mind spending a
while reading every week or so, then an amazing adventure will unfold
before you. Also, Galanda's dog is named Ellora in honour of Krysia's
Krusader. For those interested, Galanda started with the following
stats:
Galanda / priest / human / female / lawful:
St: 11   Dx: 14   Co: 10   In: 9   Wi: 17   Ch: 9
Also she started with the spell books remove curse and healing, along
with the other priest stuff (+1 mace, +0 robe, +0 small shield, 1 or 2
wolvesbane, 1 or 2 garlic, 4 potions of holy water)

---------------------------------------------
Chapter One: Welcome to the dungeon!
---------------------------------------------

Galanda stood at the entrance to the fabled ‘dungeons of doom' basking
in the sunlight. It would be a long time before she could feel the
warmth on here shoulders again. Beside her she heard a barking as her
faithful pet dog Ellora chased a butterfly eagerly. Galanda chased
after him, only catching him when he had stopped. Galanda always was
weak, preferring to focus on the arts of healing and removing cursed
placed by demons than fighting. She knew she would have to fight many
monstrous creatures before ever managing the gain the amulet of Yendor
for her mighty god Mercury, but she could learn.
"Here girl!" Galanda called out to Ellora, and Ellora came running to
her side. She took one last look at the forest scenery around here,
and walked downwards into the dungeons of doom.
Galanda's eyes took a while to adjust to the darkness, but she could
still only see a few metres in front of her. What she could see was a
strange metal object laying not far away. She recognised it almost
instantly a wand of great magical power! Galanda took a single step
forward and felt her foot land not on solid ground, but on a trap door
she had failed to notice! She jerked her foot back but it was too
late, and she started plummeting downwards.
"Aaaaaarrgh!!" Galanda screamed as she fell. Amongst her screaming a
barking could be heard, as Ellora jumped faithfully after her. Galanda
hit the ground, and the pain caused her to pass out.
When Galanda came to, she was badly injured, and had wounds on her
legs. She focussed her powers and the wounds healed themselves. What
was more worrying was that she was in a very small room, with no
obvious way of getting out. Galanda was worried and panicked, bashing
and kicking the walls. Imagine her surprise when one of them suddenly
creaked and gave way! A hidden door was smashed down and landed on the
floor. Outside Galanda could see a small, but still much larger room,
that seemed to be magically lit up. Waiting for her was Ellora, who
jumped up and start barking joyously. Galanda could see the dog was
still in pain, and healed her with her powers, then picked up some
gold she could see glinting in dirt.
After a few minutes in which Galanda focused her mind in order to gain
her powers back, Ellora began to bark angrily and dashed over to one
of the open doorways. Galanda run over and saw a large strangely
pulsing lichen. Ellora ate it, and Galanda waited. After a minute or
so, the pair continued down the corridor.
"Dang shoplifters, the nerve of them, If I lay my hands on that damn
barbarian again..." came a voice further along the corridor. Galanda
was surprised that anyone else would be in the dungeon, let alone a
cranky shopkeeper! Galanda walked along the corridor and opened a
door. Beyond it was a small collection of armour, including gloves,
boots, chain mail, and a grumpy shopkeeper. But what had drawn
Galanda's eye was a sparkling suit of crystal, obviously very high
quality. Galanda was drawn to it, and felt it's smoothness as Ellora
start playing with a pair of old gloves.
"1200 zorkmids! Pay up or get out!" called out the shop keeper.
Galanda was let down. She only had a few zorkmids she had picked up
from the floor before. Galanda glanced around looking at the various
armour, and picked up the old gloves that Ellora had been toying with.
Galanda could feel a strange power in these, as if they had been
blessed by god.
"35 zorkmids!" called out the shopkeeper. Galanda counted her gold she
had picked up. She was disappointed when she was only a few zorkmids
short. She heaved off her shield, which had been interfering with her
magic slightly.
"How much can I get for this?" Galanda asked.
"That old thing? Five at most!" The shopkeeper replied. Galanda
grudgingly accepted, and payed him all the gold she had. It was just
enough to cover the gloves. Galanda slipped on the gloves and was
surprised at how thin and pitiful they were, but she could feel
magical enchantments making them much stronger! These gloves were
surely provided much for defence than normal!
Galanda left the shop, Ellora walking behind. Galanda walked around
the dungeon level, until she found a stone staircase leading upwards.
Before that however, she had had to kill several angry newts, an
underground heard of dangerous jackals and even a fox! Galanda was
glad she had taken her spiked mace with her for protection. But with
these dangers she had also found some more gold, and even another
strange wand!
Galanda trudged up the stairs, patting Ellora, who was whining. Ellora
was not used to having to fight. As Galanda walked up the stair she
could see a familiar object in the distance, the wand that had caused
all the trouble! She dashed over to hit, bashing another lichen in her
way, and grabbed the wand. It was fashioned differently to her other
one, and was slightly curved. Galanda then began the process of
searching this level of the dungeon, and found  an unlabeled tin, a
strange key, a helmet that a pesky goblin had been wearing, a large
book, and a ring. The ring was no ordinary ring though, she could see
it held magical powers in it, and dared not put it on. As she put on
the helmet she found that it interfered with her magic, so she took it
off again. She also tried to read the book, but when she read the
first page the book disintegrated!
After Galanda had explored all the rooms she could find, she took a
long draught from a nearby water fountain. What a strange place to
find one, but she didn't mind. She was glad to find that the water was
cool and refreshing. Galanda then lead Ellora down to the third level
of this strange dungeon.
When Galanda climbed down the stairs though, she gasped. In front of
her were a large group of orcs. When they saw her they grinned,
laughed and charged at her, curved swords drawn. Galanda fled up the
stairs again, but the orcs just followed. Galanda began bashing the
nearest one with her mace, but soon she was almost surrounded. Her arm
was gashed, and she concentrated on healing the wound. Suddenly
Galanda heard a yelp of pain and an angry cry. She stopped
concentrating, and saw the Ellora had bitten and kill one of the orcs,
and the rest of them were ganging up on him. Galanda grew angry at
their coward ness at attacking the little dog, and drew out one of her
wands. She swung it in the direction of the orcs, but nothing
happened. Angrily, she drew her mace, and swung at the orcs
unprotected backs. Two cried out in pain, and one fell to the ground
dead. Ellora barked angrily and leapt at another orc. The remaining
orcs began slashing madly, but could not stand up to the anger of
Galanda, nor the fierceness of Ellora. Soon bodies littered the floor,
and Galanda slumped on the floor, focusing on healing her and Ellora's
wounds.
Soon the partners were ready, and journeyed downwards again. After the
fight with the orcs Galanda was more cautious and fought only in
corridors to avoid being surrounded. On this level of the dungeon,
Galanda discovered another shop, this one dealing in magical scrolls!
"Welcome Galanda!" greeted the shopkeeper. How he knew Galanda's name
Galanda could not fathom, but she came in, and spent a large portion
of her gold on one of the cheaper scrolls, hoping to make use of it's
magic in emergencies.
Continuing downwards, Galanda found no further shops, but did find a
large variety of weapons, including daggers, curved swords, a spear,
and even a pole arm! She did not take any though, as she had no
experience in these weapons. Other things she found were another type
of wand, an unknown scroll, two rations of food (one she ate, the
other was stowed away for later) and some boots (which she instantly
put on to make walking easier). She stopped on the fifth level of the
dungeon to rest, when she noticed something sticking out of the
ground. Upon closer investigation it was a grave of a previous
adventurer.
"RIP Christopher, killed by a rothe," read Galanda. She shivered.
Ellora yipped and ran around, which brought a smile to her face, until
there was a yelp of fear, and Ellora was silent.
Galanda jumped up in horror, and saw that Ellora was un-harmed, but
completely frozen. Tears fell from Galanda's eyes at the state of her
dog, and she quickly walked down the corridor, determined to discover
what had done this to her dog. Not far down she saw a strange green
blob, which she angrily hit with her mace. Some of the green liquid
splashed over her and burnt her skin, and also damaged her weapon!
Galanda was really angry now, and zapped her newest wand at the blob.
A long stream of fire leapt from the wand, dissolving the blob, and
burning some gloves further down the room. Galanda grinned, then
remembered her dog and ran back. What if something had found it while
she was gone? What if he had been... Galanda ran faster in fear, and
suddenly saw a huge floating eye in front of her. Galanda tried to
stop herself, but slammed into the thing, feeling it's disgusting
‘skin'. Before she could draw her mace, the floating eye glared at
Galanda, and she felt her muscles freezing. In the last instant of
conscious, she heard what sounded like something stirring and growling
in the distance, then she completely froze next to Ellora...

